    "final_answer": "I have found the definitive answer from the HuggingFace documentation for `LlamaTokenizer`. \n\n## Answer\n\nFor the `LlamaTokenizer` class in the HuggingFace Transformers library, the `spaces_between_special_tokens` parameter has the following properties:\n\n| Property | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| **Type** | `bool` |\n| **Optional** | Yes |\n| **Default Value** | `False` |\n| **Description** | Whether or not to add spaces between special tokens |\n\n### Verification Sources\n\nI confirmed this from multiple sources:\n\n1. **HuggingFace Documentation (v4.40.0)** - The `LlamaTokenizer` class signature page at `https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/v4.40.0/en/model_doc/llama#transformers.LlamaTokenizer` explicitly lists the parameter in the constructor:\n   ```\n   spaces_between_special_tokens (bool, optional, defaults to False) — Whether or not to add spaces between special tokens.\n   ```\n\n2. **Source Code** - The HuggingFace transformers GitHub source `src/transformers/models/llama/tokenization_llama.py` (v4.40.0) confirms:\n   - Constructor signature: `spaces_between_special_tokens=False`\n   - Docstring: `spaces_between_special_tokens (`bool`, *optional*, defaults to `False`): Whether or not to add spaces between special tokens.`\n\n3. **Constructor signature** from the docs page shows: `spaces_between_special_tokens = False` as one of the 12 parameters of the tokenizer.\n\nNote: In the very latest `main` branch of transformers (v4.57+), `LlamaTokenizer` was refactored to inherit from `TokenizersBackend`, and the parameter is no longer in the explicit constructor signature (it's no longer one of the 10 displayed parameters). However, for the canonical LLaMA tokenizer as documented historically, the `spaces_between_special_tokens` parameter is a `bool` with default value `False`.",
